60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option A is the most reliable. I'd know exactly when the car is mine and I could ensure it's clean for the next person.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A is a dream. No more arranging, no more untangling debts, no more evening debates. Just ""it's my day.""","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option C is the most mathematically honest. It eliminates all subsidies by charging exactly for what is used. It is the peak of equity.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option C sounds like a nightmare. We'd be arguing over every single kilometer. That's just moving the sore point to a calculator.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I love the honesty of Option C! It gives us the real figures I wanted. No more guesswork on who is driving!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, Option C still doesn't solve the ""dirty car"" problem. If we just book slots, we'll still be fighting over the state of the car.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Servas, Option C is exactly what I hate. Recording every kilometer and calculating costs? That's more admin, not less!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"While Option A is simpler, it creates a new subsidy: the person who drives less pays for the person who drives more. Is that truly fair?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, ""fair"" isn't always about the math. If Option A stops us from snapping at each other, it's fairer for our friendship.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"But wait, if we go with Option A, we're back to guessing who is using it more! I want us to be honest about the usage!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I'd rather pay a bit more and have a guaranteed, clean car on Tuesday morning than save a few yen and be stressed.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,Exactly. I'm choosing peace of mind over perfect accounting. Option A removes the mental load entirely. I'm all in.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I see the appeal of peace, but I cannot ignore the imbalance. However, if the group values harmony over precision, I will not stand in the way.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"Option B is too risky; it puts too much power on one person and creates a ""favor"" dynamic. A is the only one that breaks that cycle.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm torn. I really want the precision of C, but I don't want to be the only one fighting for it if everyone else is stressed.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Let's go with A. It's the only one that provides the stability and reliability we've been missing.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"A is the only choice for me. I'm reclaiming my evenings from the ""car coordination committee.""","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,"If we choose A, let us do so with the understanding that we are choosing a ""social subsidy"" for the sake of our collective spirit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm voting for A. It stops the ""asking for favors"" and the friction. It protects the group, which is what matters most.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"You guys have convinced me. Harmony is more important than perfect numbers. I'll vote for A too, as long as we're all happy!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
